# DevAngular333 portfolio

Static portfolio for [NamAIEngineer](https://github.com/NamAIEngineer) under the DevAngular333 product brand: a
Code2Flow Review Pack demo, public products, their evidence, and the limits of
each claim.

The deployed page is generated from `index.html` and contains no runtime data,
credentials, analytics, or external API calls.

The `review-pack-demo.html` artifact is generated from the labeled synthetic CRM
revision pair in the Code2Flow release. It stores review notes only in the
browser's local storage and exports JSON; it does not call a backend.

The Agent Teacher card points to the license-correction patch release
[`v0.1.1-devangular333`](https://github.com/NamAIEngineer/design-os-pedagogy/releases/tag/v0.1.1-devangular333); the earlier `v0.1.0-devangular333` tag remains unchanged.

The `assets/` directory contains screenshots and branded media from released
local flows: the Review Pack public demo, Agent Teacher UI, Code2Flow viewer
export, InkOS bridge smoke evidence card, graph-delta covers, a poster and a
10-second GIF preview. The full MP4 cuts and Vietnamese subtitles are attached
to the [`v0.5.3-devangular333` release](https://github.com/NamAIEngineer/design-os-code/releases/tag/v0.5.3-devangular333); the previous `v0.5.1-devangular333` release remains available as a fallback.
They are evidence images, not product mockups. The Review Pack copy names the synthetic-data boundary and deterministic focus matching; runtime behavior still requires separate human checking.

The public rerunnable capture/render guide is in the Code2Flow repository's
[`docs/media-pipeline.md`](https://github.com/NamAIEngineer/design-os-code/blob/master/docs/media-pipeline.md).
It opens the local synthetic CRM report/app with Playwright, saves raw captures
outside public repositories, and encodes the final media with FFmpeg.

Live page: <https://namaiengineer.github.io/devangular333-portfolio/>
